Attribution notes

The name ELIZA refers to Joseph Weizenbaum's 1966 program (Communications of the
ACM, 9(1):36-45). No code from that program is included here; the reference is to
the cautionary lesson about systems that are trusted because they appear to
listen.

The crisis resources named in `eliza/psyche/rt_agent.py` (988 Suicide & Crisis
Lifeline, US) are quoted as public information. This project is not affiliated
with, endorsed by, or acting on behalf of that service or any health provider.

The labelled corpus in `eliza/psyche/data/triage_corpus.jsonl` contains invented
utterances authored for this project. It contains no transcript, quotation or
paraphrase of any real person's words, and it must not be treated as a clinical
instrument or as a validation set.

No third-party runtime dependency is bundled. The Contributor Covenant text in
CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md is used under CC BY 4.0 with attribution retained at the top
of that file.
